<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<Defs>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       PYRELANDS_MECHANICS_1, mechanism 5a — the flame harvest.
       the_pyrelands.md §8: the Deep Desert Tribes are the fire's farmers; the
       burn-line is walked for scorch-fruit on their schedule.

       Cannot fire unless a burn is actually standing on the map
       (MapComponent_BurnLine.FireCount >= 10) and the Tribes are not hostile —
       when they ARE hostile what arrives is RUT_FireRaid instead. baseChance
       is generous because the gate is narrow: on a map with no fire on it, this
       incident is simply unavailable.
  ======================================================================== -->
  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>RUT_FlameHarvest</defName>
    <label>flame harvest</label>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <category>Misc</category>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.Utinni.PyrelandsMechanics.IncidentWorker_FlameHarvest</workerClass>
    <baseChance>4</baseChance>
    <minRefireDays>5</minRefireDays>
  </IncidentDef>

  <!-- ========================================================================
       PYRELANDS_MECHANICS_1, mechanism 5b — arson-justice.
       the_pyrelands.md §8, canonised: "an unplanned burn — a careless camp, a
       raider's torch, a player's mistake — is answered as arson-justice: short,
       furious Tribes raids against whoever broke the schedule."

       The gate is MapComponent_BurnLine's arson debt, which accrues ONLY for
       fires whose Fire.instigator belongs to the player. Lightning burns — the
       biome's own ruled storm loop — accrue nothing, so the Tribes never punish
       the weather. Nothing about this incident can fire on a colony that has
       not burned something.

       pointsScaleable so the storyteller supplies a sane base; the worker then
       cuts it to a fraction and forces ImmediateAttack + EdgeWalkIn, because
       the sheet says short and furious, not a siege.
  ======================================================================== -->
  <IncidentDef>
    <defName>RUT_FireRaid</defName>
    <label>fire raid</label>
    <targetTags>
      <li>Map_PlayerHome</li>
    </targetTags>
    <category>ThreatBig</category>
    <workerClass>RimMandrake.Utinni.PyrelandsMechanics.IncidentWorker_FireRaid</workerClass>
    <baseChance>8</baseChance>
    <minRefireDays>3</minRefireDays>
    <pointsScaleable>true</pointsScaleable>
    <tale>Raid</tale>
  </IncidentDef>

</Defs>
